																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13909417/scp-5640-the-stomach-idea-looking-for-greenlight">SCP-5640 The Stomach IDEA looking for greenlight</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4847512">
									

<p>I agree with Cybersqyd's perspective below&#8230; I advised tying the anomaly to the political story, but then you've gone and sorta used this political story as just background for a weird thing</p>
<p>I'm much less interested in a story about something some horrible government used to silence dissidents that is really just about the Foundation studying something&#8230; I think this would be better served with less focus on the Foundation and more on the horrors of the anomaly.</p>
<p>If this is about disappeared folks, that's a heavy narrative theme right there&#8230; don't abandon it to focus on testing with cows. The testing wouldn't be nearly as engaging as a discussion of how this government used something so horrible to enact its disappearances.</p>
<p>Finally&#8230; as Sqyd said below, because this is a real situation where real people died and were vanished by a government, you have to be careful. You don't want to make this just an entertaining story&#8230; because you're talking about a great horror perpetrated in real life. So I would suggest focusing in on that, and using the article to discuss it in a way that is meaningful.</p>

							</div>

								
					
