<p>There's a bit of info about their skill progression <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/goc-supplemental-humanoid-guide">here</a>, from a GOC perspective.</p>
<p>The <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/and-this-one-explains-humes">Hume FAQ</a> might also interest you. It also has a lot of links to reality-bender SCPs.</p>
<p>Personally I think for your &quot;standard&quot; type greens, it's mostly genetic, and their powers develop as they age.</p>
<p>Alternate idea, in abnormal psychology we have a thing we call the diathesis-stress model, where someone might have a &quot;risk factor&quot; like certain genes, but this is only &quot;activated&quot; by a major stressor/situation.</p>
<p>However, IMO there are infinite possible sources for anomalies, so you might very well see someone else with nearly-identical powers that were given to them by a God, a deal with the devil, or radiation, or magic or whatever. It's kinda up to you.</p>
<p>Edit: You can also use Tag Search in the bar on the left and search for ontokinetic and humanoid to find relevant SCPs.</p>

